  "scope": "Windows/Linux each pass 22 native suites, three full C++ workflow/batch/RGB UI regression probes, one installed public scalar/RGB C++ SDK consumer, ten background repetitions, four hidden GL contexts and 4127 installed Python checks, zero failure/error/skip. There are 334 new Python cases: 273 actual ImageJ 1.54r ColorProcessor preview/ContrastAdjuster RGB commit/subsequent-snapshot rows and 61 native API/target/guard cases. References cover every unsigned component value, all seven masks, whole/rectangular/irregular ROIs and fractional/extreme/collapsed/signed-zero spans. Native fixtures additionally verify Java numerator wrapping, three-sample ROI indexing, paired range/pixel Undo/Redo, metadata admission, stale display, mid-kernel cancellation and reentrant frozen controls. Native transaction targeting covers independent T/C/Z and whole/active/positioned masks; empty masks keep the explicit no-change/no-IO extension. Scalar API/header/V1 command contracts remain unchanged. Actual native compiled sources and installed module origins are pinned; Linux tests use a SHA-verified native snapshot of 5469 test/config/fixture files. Owned scratch and oracle/SDK build products are CRC/member-SHA archived before removal; qualified installs, consumers, probes, logs and reports remain. Original 99 requirement/status triples, existing input registrations and commercial-use dependency inventory are preserved. This is an RGB kernel/transaction/API foundation, not enabled RGB editor/captured-command/job/workflow support, complete RGB controller/stack/Auto behavior or full G057/ImageJ/Fiji/platform/resource acceptance.",
